  "rationale": "Short-term (30-day) proliferation screen: AD-bMSC-Cas9 transduced at low MOI (~0.3) with a 3,000-guide library (2,564 guides on 603 genes, 436 nc_guide non-cutting controls, each with its own nc_guideNNNNN label), 3 replicate cultures sampled at days 1-30. Counts file is the GEO UTF-16 table converted unchanged to UTF-8; column names match GSM titles one to one. The paper ran MAGeCK per day against an early reference and headlines day 30. By day 24-30 each replicate is dominated by a few clones (top 1% of guides hold 28-72% of reads; non-targeting guides reach p<0.05 at 34-61% with library totals and median-ratio totals are capped in day30 rep3), so the primary contrast is day 16 vs day 1, the last time point before clonal takeover (top-1% share 7.4-8.3%, raw control p<0.05 rate 10.4%, calibrated to 4.9%; all five TP53 guides and all four PTEN guides rise in all three replicates). Library totals are the default at this composition; median-ratio totals are a sensitivity run, and day 30 vs day 1 is kept to document the paper's headline contrast. Replicates are separate lineages after day 1 (each replicate's day-16 changes persist to day 30, r~0.7, versus ~0.2 across replicates) but the day-1 replicates are indistinguishable (r=0.995), so no replicate term."
